<title>ITALY: Olivetti starts trade in Milan up 17 pct.</title>
<headline>Olivetti starts trade in Milan up 17 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in crisit hit high-tech group Olivetti opened up 17.65 percent at 600 lire when the stock resumed trade on Thursday afternoon.</p>
<p>Bourse authorities widened the normal 10 percent trading limit to 20 percent after Olivetti repeatedly failed to resume trading after being suspended limit up after hitting the 10 percent ceiling in pre-bourse price-matching this morning.</p>
<p>The stock closed on Wednesday at 510 lire.</p>
<p>At 1303 GMT, Olivetti was quoted at 590 lire, up 15.69 percent in a generally firmer market.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129589</p>
</text>
